<p>Marketing automation sounds like something reserved for big companies with big budgets and dedicated marketing teams. It is not. At its core, marketing automation just means setting up systems that send the right message to the right person at the right time, without you having to do it manually every single time.</p>

<p>For a small business, that could be as simple as automatically sending a welcome email when someone fills out your contact form. Or texting a review request two days after an appointment. These are not complex operations. They are basic <a href="/blog/customer-follow-up-system">follow-ups</a> that most businesses know they should be doing but never get around to because the day gets away from them.</p>

<p>That is exactly the problem automation solves. Not by replacing the human element of your business, but by handling the repetitive stuff so you can focus on the work that actually needs you.</p>

